Boot from SD, and drive the console at 115200 with the real clock.

The board's first-stage loader picks its boot source from a strap it
reads at runtime; on this board that reports UART, which is not how
Tilck is booted. Take the SD path instead.

The console baud rate comes from PLAT_UART_CLK_IN_HZ and
UART_DL_BAUDRATE, whose values do not match this board's actual UART
clock, so the port comes up at the wrong rate and prints garbage.

--- a/fsbl/plat/sg200x/bl2/bl2_main.c
+++ b/fsbl/plat/sg200x/bl2/bl2_main.c
@@ -51,8 +51,8 @@
 	enum CHIP_CLK_MODE mode;
 	uint32_t v = p_rom_api_get_boot_src();
 
-	if (v == BOOT_SRC_UART) {
-		console_init(0, PLAT_UART_CLK_IN_HZ, UART_DL_BAUDRATE);
+	if (v == BOOT_SRC_SD) {
+		console_init(0, 25804800, 115200);
 	}
 
 	ATF_STATE = ATF_STATE_BL2_MAIN;
